 "answer": {
  "answer": "The study confirmed only one challenging case of the five the brief asked for, and that case is not a rear-end. On scene 19f339ba, shifting the lead car +1 s at 0.5x speed with no planner delay (S30) made every repeat fail. In each one, the policy braked hard with nothing close ahead, drifted left and clipped the car in the next lane (actor 1), not the retimed lead car. The range there only just clears the 0.5 threshold. No setting showed the policy rear-ending the lead car. The other single-run failures are hints, and two of them don't count: on 0e899dd3 (S22) the contact came from the replay before the policy took control, and on 12855a41 (S28) the ego left the road, which may be a rendering artifact. The study tried only 0.5x speed and mostly delays of zero or 200 ms, so whether other timings or speeds cause rear-ends is still untested.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "Scene 19f339ba at +1 s, 0.5x, 0 ms delay is the only confirmed challenging case: every kept repeat failed. The failure is the policy's fault but is not a rear-end. The ego braked for no clear reason, drifted about 1 m left, and its front-left corner hit actor 1 in the adjacent lane. In some runs a follower then hit it from behind.",
    "settings": [
     "S30"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The same failure, with the ego braking and clipping the left-lane car, also showed up on 19f339ba at 0 s shift in a single run. That suggests this scene fails across timings near the recorded one, but one run is only a hint.",
    "settings": [
     "S29"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The failure on 0e899dd3 at -0.5 s, 0.5x, 200 ms was not the policy's fault. The ego was still replaying the recorded path and closed on the pickup ahead, and contact was logged at the moment of handoff. The other settings on this scene had no counted failures.",
    "settings": [
     "S22",
     "S23",
     "S24",
     "S25"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The failure on 12855a41 at +2 s, 0.5x, 200 ms was the ego drifting left onto the shoulder, not a collision with the lead car. It was a single run and is flagged as a possible rendering artifact, so it does not count as a confirmed lead-vehicle case.",
